---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
import RangeField from '../../components/RangeField.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Back-of-the-envelope numbers" hint="How many tablets and tablet servers a table needs, how much of the three-level location scheme it uses, how long Chubby problems keep some data away in a year, what sorting the commit log saves at recovery, and what the paper measured. A teaching model that uses the paper's own figures where it gives them.">
  <div class="pg est" data-est>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <RangeField label="Data in the table (TB)" name="d" min="1" max="800" value="100" />
      <RangeField label="Tablet size (MB)" name="t" min="100" max="200" step="10" value="128" />
      <RangeField label="Tablets on each tablet server" name="k" min="10" max="1000" step="10" value="100" />
      <RangeField label="Tablet servers that recover a dead server's tablets" name="r" min="1" max="100" value="100" />
      <RangeField label="Tablet servers in the cluster" name="n" min="1" max="500" value="50" />
    </div>
    <dl class="est-out" data-out aria-live="polite"></dl>
    <p class="pg-note">Teaching model, with the paper's own figures where it gives them. From the paper: a tablet is split at about 100 to 200 MB by default, a server holds typically between 10 and 1000 tablets, each METADATA row takes about 1 KB and METADATA tablets are limited to 128 MB, which together allow 2 to the power 34 tablets; Chubby problems made some data unavailable for 0.0047% of server hours on average (0.0326% in the worst of 14 clusters); a Webtable experiment compressed 10 to 1 against 3 to 1 or 4 to 1 for gzip on HTML; and its random-read benchmark with 1000-byte values measured 1212, 593, 479 and 241 reads a second per server with 1, 50, 250 and 500 tablet servers. Assumptions: data is spread evenly over tablets, which are all the same size; the paper's per-server benchmark rates are shown for the nearest cluster size it measured; and a year has 8,760 hours.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, numberValue, formatOneDecimalBelow100 } from '../../playground';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-est]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const val = numberValue(q);
    const OUT_ROWS = 10; // lines in the result list
    const MB_PER_TB = 1e6, KB_PER_MB = 1000, PERCENT = 100, HOURS_PER_YEAR = 8760, SECONDS_PER_HOUR = 3600;
    const METADATA_ROW_KB = 1, METADATA_TABLET_MB = 128; // from the paper
    const MAX_TABLETS = 2 ** 34; // the paper: what the three-level scheme can address
    const CHUBBY_UNAVAILABLE_AVERAGE = 0.0047, CHUBBY_UNAVAILABLE_WORST = 0.0326; // percent of server hours, from the paper
    const COMPRESSION_GZIP = 3.5, COMPRESSION_BIGTABLE = 10; // the paper: 3 to 1 or 4 to 1 for gzip, and 10 to 1 in one Webtable experiment
    // The paper's random-read benchmark: reads a second per tablet server, by number of tablet servers.
    const RANDOM_READS: { servers: number; perServer: number }[] = [{ servers: 1, perServer: 1212 }, { servers: 50, perServer: 593 }, { servers: 250, perServer: 479 }, { servers: 500, perServer: 241 }];
    const rows = Array.from({ length: OUT_ROWS }, () => { const dt = document.createElement('dt'); const dd = document.createElement('dd'); q('[data-out]').append(dt, dd); return { dt, dd }; });
    function draw() {
      ['d', 't', 'k', 'r', 'n'].forEach((key) => (q(`[data-${key}val]`).textContent = String(val(`[data-${key}]`))));
      const dataTb = val('[data-d]'), tabletMb = val('[data-t]'), perServer = val('[data-k]'), recovering = val('[data-r]'), servers = val('[data-n]');
      const tablets = (dataTb * MB_PER_TB) / tabletMb;
      const metadataTablets = (tablets * METADATA_ROW_KB) / (METADATA_TABLET_MB * KB_PER_MB);
      const nearest = RANDOM_READS.reduce((best, row) => (Math.abs(row.servers - servers) < Math.abs(best.servers - servers) ? row : best));
      const data: [string, string][] = [
        ['Tablets the table is split into', formatOneDecimalBelow100(tablets)],
        ['Tablet servers needed at this many tablets each', formatOneDecimalBelow100(tablets / perServer)],
        ['METADATA tablets needed to locate them all (128 MB each)', formatOneDecimalBelow100(metadataTablets)],
        ['Share of the three-level scheme’s capacity used (2 to the power 34 tablets)', `${(PERCENT * tablets / MAX_TABLETS).toExponential(1)}%`],
        ['Round trips to find a tablet: empty cache, then stale cache at worst', '3, then up to 6'],
        ['Hours a year when some data is unavailable because of Chubby, on average', formatOneDecimalBelow100((CHUBBY_UNAVAILABLE_AVERAGE / PERCENT) * HOURS_PER_YEAR)],
        ['Hours a year in the worst cluster the paper measured', formatOneDecimalBelow100((CHUBBY_UNAVAILABLE_WORST / PERCENT) * HOURS_PER_YEAR)],
        ['Times the dead server’s commit log would be read without sorting it, and with sorting', `${recovering}, and 1`],
        ['Space for this table with gzip at 3.5 to 1, and at the 10 to 1 the paper saw (TB)', `${formatOneDecimalBelow100(dataTb / COMPRESSION_GZIP)} and ${formatOneDecimalBelow100(dataTb / COMPRESSION_BIGTABLE)}`],
        [`Paper: random reads a second per server, nearest measured size (${nearest.servers} servers), and for the whole cluster`, `${nearest.perServer} each, ${formatOneDecimalBelow100(nearest.perServer * nearest.servers)} in all`],
      ];
      rows.forEach((r, i) => { r.dt.textContent = data[i][0]; r.dd.textContent = data[i][1]; });
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
